experiences.description:
A senior leadership role with a critical strategic and operational leadership focus, I provided subject matter expertise to support the formulation of broader organisational strategies, whilst directing a team of 12 PMs and 2 IT PMO staff to drive the on-time and on-budget delivery of a portfolio of high-value client, product and infrastructure projects. A key contributor to the annual planning process, and participant in various internal committees tasked with championing initiatives across product development, creating competitive differentiation, improving service and driving top line growth, I spearheaded a number of continuous improvement projects and led the development of best-practice PMO frameworks to support short to medium term strategic priorities, improving performance during a period of cost control.

•	Navigated through a period of resource shortfall, making significant improvements to productivity to deliver 100% of portfolio at 70% resource capacity;
•	Focused on engagement with vendors and senior client stakeholders to identify ways of increasing top line growth and customer satisfaction through new service layers, improved customer value and new product development;
•	Consistently met operational KPIs and revenue targets, providing stable leadership during a period of change and staff recruitment to deliver over 200 projects with no high severity issues.

Tasked with maximising revenue opportunity and driving client satisfaction through operational leadership and participation in the development and execution of strategic initiatives, I built and maintained strong working partnerships across the organisation and externally to drive smooth delivery of client projects. Also focused on driving compliance and minimising client and business exposure to risk, I oversaw initial project pre-sales to ensure client requirements were fully understood and built into the project framework.

•	Increased product offering with improvements to both top and bottom line results, including overseeing delivery of a ground-breaking online pin change solution;
•	Received a business award for initiating a continuous improvement group focused on improvement of PMO frameworks;
•	2IC for VP of Delivery, stepping up provide interim leadership as acting VP of Delivery for a period of 2 months.

A front-line program management role, I led the end-to-end delivery of series of complex, business critical programs to meet organisational and client objectives. Responsible for managing all program stages from conceptualisation, design to testing and integration while also overseeing program recruitment, training and mentoring of new recruits, this was an involved people management role with a strong focus best utilising resources to achieve business objectives.

•	Directed a number of large-scale client-facing programs with teams of up to 50, including a complex, multi-project and multi vendor ATM Direct Charging Program, the success of which was recognised by a First Data Quantum Award;
•	Ensured legislative compliance with regulatory change as EMV Program Lead, overseeing delivery of 130 projects to upgrade systems and achieve vendor certification with VISA, MasterCard and Amex.

Specialising in the full lifecycle delivery of EFTPOS and EFT technology projects, I worked closely with client-side PMs to champion cost-effective, risk-adverse projects that would add value for our customer partners. A large focus of this role involved managing vendor relationships and supporting pre-sales processes to provide expertise and contribute to the design and deployment of successful customer solutions. 

•	Received Team Quantum Award for exceptional quality in delivery, managing a key project to replace Suncorp’s existing EFTPOS terminals with 3DES/Message Encryption compliant technology;
•	Project managed largest ever First Data IT project, migrating 6500 BankWest EFTPOS terminals to First Data platforms, on time and to achieve business objectives.
